editorialMd:
Build costs

Each point in this graph is a place, and each one-way path has a travel cost. Start at point 0. Find the lowest total travel cost to each point. Put these costs in point order. The cost to point 0 is 0. Record -1 for any point you cannot reach. A graph with no points gives an empty `costs`.

Return the answer

Complete `weightedLinesProofStrip` so it returns `costs`. Return it, do not print it.

Why this works

Each value in `costs` follows task 1. The later tasks use only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(V^2 + E log V); extra memory, including the helper list, O(n). n is the input length; V is the number of graph points; E is the number of graph links. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

